WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:01.801
French President Emmanuel Macron

00:00:01.801 --> 00:00:03.970
is just about to depart from China

00:00:03.970 --> 00:00:06.006
after attempting to fulfill a lofty goal

00:00:06.006 --> 00:00:07.073
to negotiate an end

00:00:07.073 --> 00:00:08.775
to the largest ground war in Europe

00:00:08.775 --> 00:00:10.377
since World War Two.

00:00:10.377 --> 00:00:12.579
Macron says he is counting on China's

00:00:12.579 --> 00:00:13.146
leader Xi

00:00:13.146 --> 00:00:15.715
Jinping to reason with Russia's

00:00:15.715 --> 00:00:17.017
president Vladimir Putin.

00:00:17.017 --> 00:00:18.218
As he tells

00:00:18.218 --> 00:00:18.785
Macron, it's,

00:00:18.785 --> 00:00:19.386
quote, in

00:00:19.386 --> 00:00:21.221
nobody's interest, unquote, for the war

00:00:21.221 --> 00:00:22.756
to drag on.

00:00:22.756 --> 00:00:24.491
Back on the battlefield, CNN's

00:00:24.491 --> 00:00:25.425
Ben Wedeman visits

00:00:25.425 --> 00:00:26.226
Ukrainian troops

00:00:26.226 --> 00:00:28.395
defending positions in the east.

00:00:28.395 --> 00:00:31.064
Armed with resolve and very,

00:00:31.231 --> 00:00:34.167
very old weapons

00:00:36.436 --> 00:00:38.538
Zhenya prepares his 50 caliber

00:00:38.538 --> 00:00:39.739
machine gun.

00:00:39.739 --> 00:00:41.775
He didn't fire this time.

00:00:41.775 --> 00:00:43.910
But he needs to be always on alert.

00:00:44.144 --> 00:00:46.179
Russian forces are nearby.

00:00:48.148 --> 00:00:48.815
This position

00:00:48.815 --> 00:00:50.083
on the northern edge of the

00:00:50.083 --> 00:00:51.251
Kharkiv region

00:00:51.251 --> 00:00:53.620
hasn't seen much action of late.

00:00:53.620 --> 00:00:54.721
But the men here

00:00:54.721 --> 00:00:56.890
have seen plenty elsewhere.

00:00:57.624 --> 00:00:58.324
In January,

00:00:58.324 --> 00:00:59.626
Zhenya was in a front line

00:00:59.626 --> 00:01:01.327
foxhole in Donbass.

00:01:01.327 --> 00:01:03.530
Withdraw from early in the morning.

00:01:03.530 --> 00:01:05.198
They would shell us with artillery,

00:01:05.198 --> 00:01:06.199
and right afterwards

00:01:06.199 --> 00:01:07.767
their infantry would try

00:01:07.767 --> 00:01:09.903
to take our positions, he recalls.

00:01:10.270 --> 00:01:11.371
You could see them.

00:01:12.338 --> 00:01:13.873
Much of the area south of here

00:01:13.873 --> 00:01:15.608
saw vicious combat.

00:01:15.608 --> 00:01:16.509
Last September,

00:01:16.509 --> 00:01:17.577
Ukrainian forces

00:01:17.577 --> 00:01:18.945
routed the Russians

00:01:18.945 --> 00:01:21.915
for much of the Kharkiv region.

00:01:21.915 --> 00:01:22.982
Before retreating,

00:01:22.982 --> 00:01:24.384
they toppled the Soviet

00:01:24.384 --> 00:01:26.553
era communications tower.

00:01:26.553 --> 00:01:27.787
Scorched earth.

00:01:27.787 --> 00:01:29.923
Their tactic of choice.

00:01:29.923 --> 00:01:30.723
This position

00:01:30.723 --> 00:01:32.792
manned by the 209th battalion

00:01:32.792 --> 00:01:33.960
of the Ukrainian Army's

00:01:33.960 --> 00:01:37.497
113th Brigade, is holding steady.

00:01:38.031 --> 00:01:38.731
Defense,

00:01:38.731 --> 00:01:41.134
not offense, is the order of the day.

00:01:42.102 --> 00:01:44.070
Aleksey was a nuclear physicist

00:01:44.070 --> 00:01:45.872
before picking up a gun.

00:01:45.872 --> 00:01:47.907
We have enough ammunition

00:01:47.907 --> 00:01:50.076
and we have enough weapon and

00:01:52.212 --> 00:01:54.781
different armor equipment.

00:01:55.448 --> 00:01:57.851
But it's all for defense

00:01:59.285 --> 00:02:00.987
equipment for the counterattack.

00:02:00.987 --> 00:02:02.589
It will be better

00:02:02.589 --> 00:02:05.792
because if he is on the free, I will have

00:02:08.061 --> 00:02:10.029
the weapons they have are hardly

00:02:10.029 --> 00:02:11.364
the latest.

00:02:11.364 --> 00:02:12.332
The troops showed us

00:02:12.332 --> 00:02:15.135
a Swedish made recoilless rocket launcher

00:02:15.368 --> 00:02:18.204
dating back to 1978.

00:02:19.172 --> 00:02:20.373
They defend their position

00:02:20.373 --> 00:02:22.475
with other decades old methods

00:02:23.009 --> 00:02:24.811
beyond this razor wire.

00:02:24.811 --> 00:02:27.614
Just on the other side are landmines

00:02:28.214 --> 00:02:28.982
Fortunately,

00:02:28.982 --> 00:02:31.851
this area is relatively quiet,

00:02:33.052 --> 00:02:34.187
which is a welcome

00:02:34.187 --> 00:02:36.890
respite for these battle scarred troops.

00:02:37.690 --> 00:02:39.125
Stumbled was a nightmare

00:02:39.125 --> 00:02:40.627
is how you have gone describes

00:02:40.627 --> 00:02:42.362
the battle in the dead of winter

00:02:42.362 --> 00:02:43.429
in Donbas.

00:02:43.429 --> 00:02:45.798
I'll remember it for the rest of my life.

00:02:46.533 --> 00:02:47.400
52 year

00:02:47.400 --> 00:02:49.235
old Vitaly served with Russians

00:02:49.235 --> 00:02:51.037
in the Soviet army.

00:02:51.037 --> 00:02:53.573
This war has severed all ties.

00:02:54.340 --> 00:02:56.709
The youth we ate from the same pot,

00:02:56.709 --> 00:02:58.711
he says, reminiscing of his days

00:02:58.711 --> 00:03:00.647
as a young recruit.

00:03:00.647 --> 00:03:01.881
That was then.

00:03:01.881 --> 00:03:04.417
This is now, after so many battles.

00:03:04.651 --> 00:03:07.654
They prepare for the next Ben Wedeman,

00:03:07.654 --> 00:03:10.190
CNN, in the northern Kharkiv region.

00:03:11.024 --> 00:03:13.326
And our thanks to Ben Wedeman in Ukraine.

00:03:13.726 --> 00:03:14.794
In Russia, authorities

00:03:14.794 --> 00:03:16.262
have formally charged

00:03:16.262 --> 00:03:16.696
Wall Street

00:03:16.696 --> 00:03:17.397
Journal reporter

00:03:17.397 --> 00:03:19.699
Evan Gursky book with espionage.

00:03:19.732 --> 00:03:21.134
That's according to Russian state media,

00:03:21.134 --> 00:03:22.869
which added that he continues

00:03:22.869 --> 00:03:24.237
to deny the accusation.

00:03:24.237 --> 00:03:24.938
Secretary of State

00:03:24.938 --> 00:03:26.139
Antony Blinken told reporters

00:03:26.139 --> 00:03:28.441
on Wednesday that there's no doubt

00:03:28.441 --> 00:03:30.343
he's being wrongfully detained.

00:03:30.343 --> 00:03:32.412
Gersh Kovac is a journalist, not a spy.

00:03:32.412 --> 00:03:34.380
He was detained by Russian authorities

00:03:34.380 --> 00:03:37.850
last week ludicrously accused of spying.

00:03:37.884 --> 00:03:39.185
This is the first time

00:03:39.185 --> 00:03:39.619
it's happened

00:03:39.619 --> 00:03:40.553
to an American journalist

00:03:40.553 --> 00:03:42.822
since the end of the Cold War.

00:03:42.822 --> 00:03:43.256
The Wall Street

00:03:43.256 --> 00:03:44.324
Journal released this statement

00:03:44.324 --> 00:03:45.959
after reports emerged the first group

00:03:45.959 --> 00:03:47.260
which had been formally charged.

00:03:47.260 --> 00:03:47.427
Quote,

00:03:47.427 --> 00:03:49.662
These charges are categorically false

00:03:49.662 --> 00:03:50.930
and unjustified

00:03:50.930 --> 00:03:52.899
and we continue to demand Evans

00:03:52.899 --> 00:03:54.601
immediate release, unquote.

00:03:54.601 --> 00:03:55.101
Russian state

00:03:55.101 --> 00:03:56.803
media says a Moscow court

00:03:56.803 --> 00:03:59.305
will hear an appeal filed by Herskovitz

00:03:59.305 --> 00:04:01.441
his lawyers against his arrest

00:04:01.441 --> 00:04:03.543
later this month. What a travesty.

